### 04.05.2026 #################################################################
  - change in usage MERIC_SAMPLES [boolean] (false), and new input parameter MERIC_SAMPLING_FREQUENCY [Hz] (0)
  - MERIC Python module generation if pybind is detected at the MERIC configure stage
  - fixed MPI support in Python
  - fixed check of the allowed GPU SM frequency (NVIDIA GPUs) interval for frequency tuning
  - improved power monitoring system availability detection
  - systemInfo detailed output on available power monitoring systems
  - MERICext support for HWMON energy measurement
  - solved Blade error output of non-HDEEM power monitoring systems
  - removed requirement to store power samples to evaluate energy consumption from HWMON power sampling
  - MERIC does no longer recognize power monitoring systems HWMON-S and HWMON-C, but only unified HWMON
  - support for monitoring of performance counters on Fujitsu A64FX using perfevent and evaluation of corresponding metrics
  - support for energy measurement from PDUs exposing the power samples to user space 
  - MERIC E4 Remote node monitoring utility with E4 PDU sampling support
  - new CUDA test application
  - support for additional Fortran compilers

### 17.12.2025 #################################################################
  - MERIC_TMP_PATH should be defined in configuration stage to specify where to store temporary files
  - support for power sampling (use MERIC_SAMPLES to specify sampling frequency [Hz]), current support for HWMON, RAPL and NVML
  - new python module for MERIC usage with python applications
  - new static tool supporting multi-node energy measurement, and energy counters overflow handling
  - support for Nvidia Grace/Grace Hopper energy and power sampling using HWMON and NVML
  - support for AMD MI250X energy measurement and frequency scaling using AMD ROCm
  - support for Intel and AMD RAPL energy readings from the intel_rapl / intel_rapl_common kernel module 
  - support for Intel and AMD RAPL energy readings using perf
  - support for AMD RAPL energy readings using amd_energy interface
  - support for measurements with a long runtime using RAPL (multiple overflow handling)
  - support for automatic thread pinning using MERIC_PIN_MODE
  - new MERICext library exposing energy measurement for 3rd party tools
  - support for Intel Sapphire Rapids uncore frequency monitoring
  - unified set of power management metrics in supported hardware platforms
  - performance counters reading using perf is now the default interface for metric (MERIC_COUNTERS=perfevent), requires paranoid level = 0

### 15.05.2024 #################################################################
  - MERIC_MeasureStop and MERIC_MeasureStopStart now requires name of the region to stop
  - MERIC_MODE and MERIC_CONTINUAL options have been replaced by MERIC_MEASURE, comma separated list of measurement options
  - removed MERIC_ITERATION input parameter, it is generated automatically
  - support for Intel CPU core frequency scaling under Intel Hardware Performance State (HWP)
  - support for Intel CPU core frequency scaling under intel_cpufreq scalig diver
  - support for Nvidia GPUs energy measurement using NVML (MERIC_MEASURE=NVML)
  - support Nvidia GPUs power capping, streaming multiprocessors and memory frequency tuning
  - support for AMD RAPL energy measurement (available from Zen architecture)
  - support AMD Zen CPUs core frequency tuning using msr_safe
  - support AMD EPYC CPUs core frequency tuning and power capping using Host System Management Port (HSMP) kernel module + EPYC System Management Interface (E-SMI) In-band Library
  - support IBM OpenPOWER OCC firmware for energy measurement (MERIC_MEASURE=OCC)
  - support Fujitsu A64FX energy measurement (MERIC_MEASURE=A64FX)
  - new MERICwrapper tool, that provides state space search and analysis of already measured data instead of the RADAR
  - static tools for energy measurement support not only RAPL but NVML too
  - implemented system topology detection
  - powercap is now set in milliwatts and milliseconds instead of watts and microseconds
  - RAPL now provides the energy consumption in double data type
  - new MERIC_COUNTERS=msr - CPU core and uncore frequency, and RAPL activity monitoring, using libmsr
  - fixed restore of the system hardware settings in the energyMeasureStop
  - improved systemInfo tool
		+ extended amount of the reported information, including the system topology
		+ provides possibility to restore the system settings
  - HW tuning and RAPL energy measurement using GEOPM
  - continual mode is now default
  - it is not necessary any more to set MERIC_CONTINUAL for energy measurement systems that does not support non-continual measurement
  - unified output label for all the energy measurement systems
  - removed the duty to compile MERIC with numactl when libmsr, x86_adapt, and GEOPM not available
  - compiler detection has been added, if not recognized, the default compiler is GNU (instead of Intel compiler, which was default previously)
  - SBI tools are compiled together with MERIC when using GNU compiler (Dyninst must be compiled using GNU compiler)
  - all the MERIC's utilities are located in the tools directory, the source files re-located
  - new format of the file that keeps the default settings, now supports multiple architectures from one installation
  - it is possible to use MERIC without libmsr, with direct access to msr_safe
  - MERIC output when no parameter is tuned is now default.csv instead of log.csv
  - new option MERIC_OUTPUT_FORMAT
  - RAPL power limit time window description changed from Twindow to CPUPWRtw
  - (power) samples are stored juts once in a separate directory
  - readex.h dropped from the MERIC repository, the feature of multi-tools instrumentation provides Instrument API, test cases now use MERIC API only
  - TIMEPROF library now allows to collect runtime of regions by all processes, and checks that the regions have been executed by all processes the same number of times (TIMEPROF_MASTER=0).
  - simplified MERIC configuration file
		- removed socket-/node-specific tuning
		- removed configuration change threshold
		+ added minimum region runtime filtering
  - utilities are stored into bin/ directory

### 30.04.2019 #################################################################
  - new Static Binary Instrymentation (SBI) tool for MERIC instrumentation
  - user should not specify value of requested CPU core frequency, uncore frequency and number of active threads in the name of the output file any more - it is done automatically
  - MERIC supports Intel RAPL PKG power capping - MERIC_PWRCAP_POWER and MERIC_PWRCAP_TIME must be set to run an instrumented application
  - together with MERIC_Init() starts automatically a first region and ends with MERIC_Close()
  - directory with measured data contain measurementInfo.json, for data description
  - new MERIC API RAII function for scope measurement MERIC_captureScope(const char * region)
  - barriers turn off available not only for production runs
  - new MERIC mode to store regions runtime only
  - support for IBM OpenPOWER8+ CINECA D.A.V.I.D.E. cluster energy measurement and DFVS
  - MERIC_MeasureStop() and MERIC_MeasureStopStart() now returns runtime of the stopped region
  - new function runtime profiling library TIMEPROF is now part of the repository
  - now on request available compilation of MERIC/TIMEPROF MPI version without OpenMP
  - test/environment_taurus updated and renamed to test/environment_default.source
  - default MERIC mode is RUN (3) instead of HDEEM (0)
  - CPU core and uncore frequency may be specified without unit in Hz or with unit
  - removed mericMeasurementCounters - when runing an application several times with the same configuration MERIC_ITERATION=$iteration must be exported
  - support for libmsr RAPL reading, DVFS, UFS and power cap
  - systemInfo - new tool to show system parameters limits
  - energyMeasureStart/Stop tuning the same system parameteres as MERIC
  - energyMeasureStart/Stop now compile together with MERIC

### 05.06.2018 #################################################################
  - fixed single RAPL overflow
  - HDEEM error handled without writing zero values into output files
  - MERIC_FREQUENCY and MERIC_UNCORE_FREQUENCY should be set to zero for default run
  - ARM Jetson/TX1 energy measurement and frequency scaling
  - ARM ThunderX energy measument support (DVFS not available)
  - tested and adapted for Intel KNL
  - tool for static energy measurement and CPU frequencies change
  - updated shared Score-P/Meric header file
		+ readex.h has new functions for region define (with backward compatibility)
		+ support for the rest of Score-P API
		+ added Fortran version readex.inc
  - new templated version of store classes - please check your RADAR configuration files for changes in labels in MERIC output files
  - added ignore functions to turn off measurement
  - default output directory name changed from hdeemMeasurement to mericMeasurement
  - fixed cpu frequency setting in case of using region options
  - if x86adapt is not available, compilation with -lnuma is required
  - Fortran meric_fortran_interface.h90 renamed to meric.inc
  - MERIC MPI now works in MERIC_AGGREGATE mode as default
  - removed duty for c++14 standart
  - reduced MERIC overhead
  - new MERIC function MERIC_MeasureStopStart to avoid extra environment switching
  - analysis data directory should contain file measurementInfo.json that describes the test
  - new possibility to turn off MPI or OpenMP barriers for production runs
  - updated labels in output files
  - removed dummy compilation without HDEEM
  - updated README

### 10.04.2017 #################################################################
  - added Fortran interface
  - repaired measurement based on HDEEM samples - no Meric warnings about hdeem frequency
  - added computational intensity measurement
  - much faster Meric IO
  - new warnings when regions are too short
  - handles RAPL overflow
  - added shared Score-P/MERIC api
  - MERIC_NUM_THREADS is now obligatory parameter
  - input region options json file is now parsed via sheredom library which is much more accurate in input file format
  - completely new way of work with region options, that gives much more options to set - see the README "MERIC input parameters" section!
		+ Meric does not switch the environment during runtime if region options is not set
  		+ per node and per socket settings
  		+ user-defined list of regions and size of change of settings to ignore
  		+ different default settings
  - updated error messages
  - freeipmi library is not needed to compile Meric without HDEEM
  
### 02.02.2017 #################################################################
  - git repository moved from git@code.it4i.cz:xvysoc01/meric.git to git@code.it4i.cz:vys0053/meric.git
  - update from hdeem/2.2.2 to hdeem/2.2.20ms
  - now requires c++14 standart
  - rapl counters
  - it is now possible to use hdeem, rapl and counters at one time
  - MERIC works in modes - export MERIC_MODE, see README
  - new compilation dummy mode (make dummy) - it is possible to turn off hdeem and use the rest of the library
  - papi and perfevent counters now gives correct values for MPI code
  - in test folder is an environment script to set MERIC variables
  - region.options file is not loaded implicitly, but user have to set MERIC_REGION_OPTIONS environment variable
  - MERIC prints its output about its progress only when configured with --verbose (make ddt)
  - to reduce content of output files, Meric doesn't print hdeem samples, if MERIC_SAMPLES=1 is not set
  - when using counters, there is also an information about flop/s  
  - enhanced version of run.sh 

### 23.11.2016 #################################################################
  - CPU core frequency is set in 0.1 GHz instead of Hz
  - region.options file format changed to JSON
  - counters store - a possibility to store HW counters values using papi or perfevent
  - set number of threads for each region using MERIC_NUM_THREADS variable
  - tests in test folder are renamed and blas test is added
  - connection to RADAR tool, that is set by default to run with MERIC test.cpp and test_mpi.cpp examples
  - HDEEM measurement counters are moved to separated folder, that has the same name as MERIC_OUTPUT_DIR with suffix "Counters"


